<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enlil-bani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1860–1837 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enlil-bani was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin-dynasty">Isin dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in the 19th century BCE. Later Babylonian chronicles tell that he was a gardener installed by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erra-imitti">Erra-imitti</a> as a substitute king to avert an evil omen; when Erra-imitti died suddenly, Enlil-bani kept the throne. He ruled for about 24 years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enlil-bani.jpg" alt="Enlil-bani" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foundation_Cone_of_Enlil-Bani..JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
